Z||000001||ironhedno3||01-31-2001||07:42 PM||||use the crank from a large journal 2.8 crank..say 86 and up..all were internally balanced after 88..dont know about pistons cause 3.4 has the bigger bore of all 60 degree v6's||||reg||1
Z||000002||lou_dias||01-31-2001||09:20 PM||||You have to get longer rods... 32 hundreth's of an inch longer than stock to be exact if you are going to use 3.4 pistons.  you might as well use the 3.4 DTOC engine's pistons to get more compression.  What you would have is a 3.0 Liter engine.  The 3.4's don't have a problem revving higher, that depends more on your breathing ability and the durability of your components more than your bore to rod length ratio.  If you really want to rev your engine, the 3.4 TDOC redlines at 7000rpm and supposedly can really go to 8000 with some reprogramming.||||reg||1
